// SWARM RABBIT HOLE — Wave 13 (Impl-R): read_J's ordering discipline
// (W2B §3: "read_J(c) (fallback, ordered after J(W): fold-valued,
// schedule-independent)"). The fold-valued claim is TEMPORAL: it
// holds only where J(W) provably happened. Before the wave the cell
// holds κ₀ only — a read there is read_S (schedule-dependent class),
// whatever it is named; the checker refuses the mislabeling and
// points at the honest mode. MUST FAIL TO COMPILE.

ptr c = lcell_new(0)

fn main() {
    lcell_inflate(c, 7, 0)

    // read_J BEFORE the wave: the fold hasn't happened — the value
    // is not yet fold-valued. The read mode is read_S here.
    print(read_J(c))

    wave {
        contrib(c, 9, 0)
    }
    print("unreachable")
}
